The node body is below. I left out both operations requests (the log-file append and the metadata fetch). The node's contract grants only `LLMClient<inference>`, so its world imports only `aap:caps/inference-llm`. The target has no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem or HTTP import to call. Writing to `/var/log/...` or fetching the metadata URL would need new capabilities in the graph, such as `http-client`, plus a host-side logging facility. The input text would also be sent to an outside service, which should be an explicit graph-level decision. The node's output is unaffected.

